From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Report VFE and CSID errors, fail the queues of a wedged VFE

Decode the error interrupts the vendor driver takes on Titan 175: VFE
status 0 0x3fc00 and status 1 0xefff7e80, bus composite error,
overwrite, overflow and violation, and on the CSID the D-PHY receiver
errors and the IPP and RDI FIFO overflows, which camss left masked or
ignored. Each marks the buffer of the frame being written with
VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR; a dual IFE slave passes its stripe's error on to
the master's buffer of that frame. More than 16 within 100 ms turn the
error interrupts off until the next stream start, as a wedged write
master raises them continuously.

After one frame with a bus error the pixel path writes nothing more
until the stream restarts: the hardware does not recover by itself, as
in the vendor driver. Make every queue a wedged VFE feeds fail with
vb2_queue_error(): its lines' video nodes, the parameters and statistics
nodes, and with dual IFE the master's queues when the slave wedges.
Userspace sees EPOLLERR and -EIO, stops and starts the streams, which
resets the VFE. The VFE error interrupts and the CSID FIFO overflows (or
a storm of CSID errors) are fatal this way; CSI2 receiver CRC and ECC
errors only fail their frame.

Tested with a write master's buffer height halved for one frame (single
IFE, dual IFE with the master or the slave faulted) and with CSID
receiver errors set by software: the streams restart within 60-70 ms
and frames continue.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
